    "title": "Jacksonville celebrates July as Park and Recreation Month",
    "text": "Donna Deegan - Mayor of Jacksonville, FL | City of Jacksonville website\nDonna Deegan - Mayor of Jacksonville, FL | City of Jacksonville website\nJuly is celebrated as Park and Recreation Month across the nation, recognizing the important role of parks, trails, open spaces, and recreation programs in improving life quality for individuals, families, and communities.\nIn Jacksonville, projects such as the Emerald Trail are reshaping how residents navigate and experience the city. This 30-mile urban trail system connects neighborhoods, parks, schools, and cultural sites while promoting equity, mobility, and environmental sustainability.\nMayor Deegan invites all residents to explore and support these community assets that contribute to making Jacksonville a place \"Where You Belong.\"\nORGANIZATIONS IN THIS STORY\n!RECEIVE ALERTS\nSign-up\nDONATE\nDonate",
